#
# WHY A COPY AT ALL, since a copy is the thing that drifts. This workflow runs on
# a GitHub runner that never checks out qontinui-claude-config, so it cannot
# source the library. The alternatives were weighed and rejected: checking out
# the config repo as a sibling would let one config-repo edit red three unrelated
# repos, and publishing the oracle as a composite action is a distribution
# project rather than a line of CI. Inlining is what coord already does and what
# visibly works; the cost is transcription drift, which is mechanically
# checkable, so it is checked.
#
# Output: "<tests_ran> <summary_lines>" on one line, always, exit 0 always.
# Reads BOTH grammars — libtest `test result: ok. N passed;` and nextest
# `Summary [...] N tests run:` — because coord's own shipped floor anchors
# /^test result: ok\./ and matches the nextest line nowhere, which is why the
# job that needed a floor most had none.
